{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Winter brings a familiar rhythm to Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge in New Mexico. The cranes arrive, wetlands fill with birds and this area becomes a hub for seasonal wildlife. Established in 1939, the 57,331-acre sanctuary was created to provide a protected stopover for migrating waterfowl. Its wetlands, fields and waterways now support wildlife throughout the year. Sandhill cranes, seen in today's image, are especially associated with the refuge during winter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_ROW2927926233_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_ROW2927926233_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sandhill cranes, Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Terry St.Louis/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sandhill+Cranes&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261030_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes"},"Ssd":"20261030","Name":"AutumnCranes","Market":"ROW","Hash":"2927926233","FullDateString":"30 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning mist drifts among the standing stones of Avebury in Wiltshire, England, the scene feels almost timeless. These ancient megaliths form part of one of the world's most remarkable prehistoric landscapes, centred on a vast Neolithic monument built around 4,500 years ago. Avebury contains the world's largest prehistoric stone circle, as well as a massive henge and stone avenues extending into the surrounding countryside. Together with nearby monuments such as Silbury Hill and West Kennet Avenue, it forms part of an extensive Neolithic complex that has fascinated generations of visitors, researchers and archaeologists.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_ROW2156116179_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_ROW2156116179_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Standing stones at Avebury in Wiltshire, England","Copyright":"© George W Johnson/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Avebury+henge+Wiltshire&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261029_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones"},"Ssd":"20261029","Name":"AveburyStones","Market":"ROW","Hash":"2156116179","FullDateString":"29 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What stories could these walls tell? Rising above eastern Bohemia in Czechia, Kunětická hora Castle has witnessed centuries of history. Dating to the late 14th century, the castle gradually evolved into an impressive fortress and noble residence. Its elevated position offered commanding views of the surrounding countryside and helped make it an important stronghold.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_ROW1907560324_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_ROW1907560324_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Kunětická hora Castle, Bohemia, Czechia","Copyright":"© Marek Saroch/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Kun%c4%9btick%c3%a1+hora+Castle&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261028_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle"},"Ssd":"20261028","Name":"KuneticeCastle","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1907560324","FullDateString":"28 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in calm water and glowing in the light of the setting sun, this grove of pond cypress creates a striking display of colour and symmetry. Native to the south-eastern United States, the species is associated with shallow ponds, depressions and wetland habitats. This image was captured in Georgia, where these trees can be found in places such as the Okefenokee Swamp and other low-lying wetlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_ROW1830221412_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_ROW1830221412_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A grove of pond cypress trees with autumn foliage, Georgia, United States","Copyright":"© Chris Moore/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pond+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261027_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress"},"Ssd":"20261027","Name":"PondCypress","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1830221412","FullDateString":"27 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Bulgaria's Western Rhodope Mountains, autumn leaves gather beside the rushing waters of Sitovo Waterfall. Near the village of Sitovo, southwest of Plovdiv, the falls tumble beneath an old stone bridge whose arch frames the cascades like a storybook scene. Moss-covered stones and pine trees add shades of green to the autumn landscape, while fallen leaves gather along the water's edge or drift through its pools. The falls become especially lively after rain and during spring snowmelt, when the surrounding woodland echoes with the sound of rushing water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_ROW1586593105_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_ROW1586593105_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Autumn waterfalls near Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria","Copyright":"© Nadya85/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sitovo+Plovdiv+Bulgaria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261026_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall"},"Ssd":"20261026","Name":"SitovoWaterfall","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1586593105","FullDateString":"26 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When night falls in Jasper National Park, Alberta, Canada, the mountains get a whole new backdrop. Designated a Dark-Sky Preserve in 2011, the park spans more than 11,000 square kilometres, with measures in place to reduce light pollution. Here, the stars, planets and the Milky Way put up a celestial show, giving visitors a reason to look up. Then morning arrives and the focus shifts from the sky above to the landscape below.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_ROW1322674228_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_ROW1322674228_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Maligne Lake, Jasper National Park, Alberta, Canada","Copyright":"© Andrey Popov/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_MaligneFest\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jasper+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_MaligneFest"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"MaligneFest","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1322674228","FullDateString":"25 okt. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In much of Brazil, July is synonymous with cold weather, mist and muted tones. The green-headed tanager goes in the opposite direction. Green, blue, turquoise, yellow, black, orange and touches of violet come together on a body just over 13 centimetres long, appearing among the branches like a living argument for extravagance. It is no surprise that it frequently features on lists of the most beautiful birds in the world.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Tanager_ROW0977269473_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Tanager_ROW0977269473_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Green-headed tanager","Copyright":"© Juan Carlos Vindas/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261024_Tanager\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Green-headed+tanager&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261024_Tanager"},"Ssd":"20261024","Name":"Tanager","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0977269473","FullDateString":"24 okt. 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A volcano, a rainforest and a bamboo grove? Haleakalā National Park on Maui has all three. Spanning Maui from its 3,055-metre summit to the coast, the park protects landscapes that change dramatically with elevation, rainfall and temperature. It was established in 1916 as part of Hawaii National Park and became its own national park in 1961. The name Haleakalā translates to 'House of the Sun', reflecting the Hawaiian mo'olelo of Māui capturing the sun to lengthen the day.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_ROW6967541605_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_ROW6967541605_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261106_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6967541605","FullDateString":"6 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A simple wooden stile leads into one of England's most celebrated landscapes. The Lake District, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is a patchwork of shimmering lakes, rugged fells and centuries-old stone walls, all shaped by both nature and farming traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_ROW6736786838_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_ROW6736786838_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Wooden stile at a stone wall, Black Crag, Lake District, England","Copyright":"© Alex Treadway/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+District&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261105_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing"},"Ssd":"20261105","Name":"StileCrossing","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6736786838","FullDateString":"5 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People paddle through a glowing maze of bald cypress in Xuancheng, Anhui, where autumn transforms flooded woodlands into a tapestry of amber, copper and deep rust. Known scientifically as 'Taxodium distichum', bald cypress is unusual among conifers because it sheds its soft, feathery needles each fall, turning reddish-brown before they drop.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_ROW3959002694_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_ROW3959002694_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"People rowing among colourful bald cypress, Xuancheng, Anhui, China","Copyright":"© Jackal Pan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=bald+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261104_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina"},"Ssd":"20261104","Name":"AutumnChina","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3959002694","FullDateString":"4 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On Brazil's southern coast, Taquaras Beach offers a quieter escape in Balneário Camboriú, Santa Catarina. Clear blue-green waters meet a broad stretch of golden sand, backed by lush vegetation and rolling green hills. Away from the livelier atmosphere of the city centre, the beach is known for its peaceful surroundings and natural beauty. With its inviting shoreline, rich greenery and unspoilt feel, Taquaras showcases a calmer side of this popular Brazilian coastal destination.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Camburiu_ROW3589076688_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Camburiu_ROW3589076688_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Taquaras Beach, Balneário Camboriú, Brazil","Copyright":"© MaRabelo/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261103_Camburiu\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Balne%c3%a1rio+Cambori%c3%ba&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261103_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261103_Camburiu"},"Ssd":"20261103","Name":"Camburiu","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3589076688","FullDateString":"3 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These polar bears are gathering along the shores of Hudson Bay in Manitoba, Canada, waiting for sea ice to form so they can head back out to hunt seals. Polar bears are powerful swimmers, expert hunters and remarkably adapted to life in one of Earth's harshest environments. Yet shrinking sea ice means many spend longer on land, making it harder to find food and raising the risk of encounters with people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_ROW5956466149_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_ROW5956466149_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Polar bear and cubs by Hudson Bay, Manitoba, Canada","Copyright":"© Danita Delimont/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Polar+bear&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261102_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear"},"Ssd":"20261102","Name":"HudsonBear","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5956466149","FullDateString":"2 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're enjoying the misty views sweeping across the Black Forest, which stretches for around 160 kilometres across south-west Germany, bringing together wooded hills, deep valleys, lakes and charming towns. Its highest point, Feldberg, rises to 1,493 metres, while the Black Forest is also the starting point for the Danube and Neckar rivers. There's plenty of history and tradition here too. Forestry has long played an important role in the region, while its centuries-old clockmaking heritage helped make the distinctive cuckoo clock famous far beyond Germany.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_ROW3364796116_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_ROW3364796116_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg, Germany","Copyright":"© Britus/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Black+Forest+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261101_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261101","Name":"SchwarzwaldAutumn","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3364796116","FullDateString":"1 nov. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lake Braies sits almost 1,500 metres above sea level in the Dolomites of South Tyrol, northern Italy. Surrounded by forest and the dramatic peaks of the Fanes-Sennes-Braies Nature Park, the lake is known for its striking green and blue waters. A 3.5-kilometre trail circles the shore, while traditional wooden rowing boats offer another way to take in the scenery. The lake is also a starting point for several mountain walks, including the Dolomites' famous Alta Via 1.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_ROW3051494546_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_ROW3051494546_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park, Dolomites, Italy","Copyright":"© leonid_tit/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261031_AlpineBraies